    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1">

                <pb facs="0101" n="1" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg1"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Earle, George H./31: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Earle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-28T13:00:00+01:00">October 28, 1933—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 28—11:10 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>60. I am leaving tomorrow, Sunday, with Kliefoth<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1-f1"/>
                    and Military Attaché<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1-f2"/> for 14 days trip of
                    observation through 9 Austrian provincial capitals calling on governors and
                    officials. Austrian Foreign Office pleased with this trip. Will have frequent
                    telephonic communication with Swift at Legation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Earle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1-f1-content">
                <p>Alfred W. Kliefoth, First Secretary of Legation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1-f2-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Martin C. Shallenberger.</p>
            </note>
